<div class="quick-card-val">5.8–6.4s</div>
<div class="quick-card-sub">General population, no specific sprint training</div>
</div>
</div>
<p>These ranges represent 16-year-olds with normal athletic activity but no dedicated speed training. Varsity athletes who play speed-dependent sports typically run 0.3 to 0.5 seconds faster than the population average.</p>
<p>Sixteen is sophomore year for most athletes — the point where camps, combines, and early recruiting evaluations start paying attention, even though the bulk of scholarship offers are still a year or two away. <strong>What you run at 16 tells scouts less about where you are and more about where you're headed.</strong></p>

